# {{ project_name }}

A cross-platform C++{{ cpp_standard }} library using CMake, vcpkg, and GoogleTest.

## Reproducible setup and validation

From a fresh checkout:

```bash
python scripts/bootstrap.py
python scripts/validate.py
```

Requires Python 3.12+, Git and a platform C++17 toolchain (GCC/Clang on Linux; Visual Studio 2022 C++ tools and a Windows SDK on Windows). Linux also needs curl, zip, unzip and tar. Bootstrap installs pinned tools and the declared vcpkg baseline in `.dev-tools`. Validation configures, builds the static/shared libraries and example, and runs CTest.

The scripts supply tool paths automatically, including Ninja inside vcpkg compiler detection. Compiler tracking remains enabled. No shell activation or manual path setup is required.

## Build presets

Validation uses `windows-vcpkg` / `windows-release` / `windows-release-tests` on Windows and `linux-vcpkg-release` / `linux-release` / `linux-release-tests` on Linux. Windows uses Visual Studio 2022; Linux uses Ninja. `CMakePresets.json` also contains Debug presets. Keep preset changes aligned with `scripts/validate.py`.

## Dependencies and overlay ports

`vcpkg.json` declares project dependencies. The generated `vcpkg-configuration.json` uses Microsoft vcpkg as the only package registry and declares the repository-local `vcpkg-ports` directory as an overlay.

The `gtest` dependency is resolved from `vcpkg-ports/gtest` before registry lookup. This local port preserves the official GoogleTest build and standard `GTest::*` CMake targets, but configures pkg-config metadata with `SKIP_CHECK`, so vcpkg does not acquire or execute `pkgconf`.

No personal vcpkg registry is required. When the custom recipe changes, update the files under `vcpkg-ports/gtest` and validate the project on Windows and Linux. All other package names continue to resolve from the Microsoft default registry.

## Continuous integration

Pushing this project to GitHub automatically runs `.github/workflows/build-and-test.yml` on Windows and Linux. Pull requests and manual runs also trigger it. The workflow invokes `python scripts/bootstrap.py` and `python scripts/validate.py`; those scripts build the libraries, examples and tests, check that `pkgconf` was neither installed nor acquired, and run CTest.

To add another dependency:

```bash
vcpkg add port <package-name>
```

The package resolves from Microsoft vcpkg unless a same-named local port exists under `vcpkg-ports`.

## Template updates

Commit `.copier-answers.yml` and project changes before `copier update --vcs-ref <template-tag>`. Template Git tags version updates independently of your project's version.
